.TH V7AS 1
.SH NAME
v7as, v7as2 \- PDP-11 assembler, pass 1 and pass 2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v7as
[
.B \-
] [
.B \-u
] [
.BI \-o " objfile"
]
.I "file ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I as
is the V7 Unix PDP-11 assembler, translated from its original assembly
sources
.RI ( as11.s .. as19.s
for pass 1,
.IR as21.s .. as29.s
for pass 2) into C so it runs host-side as a cross-assembler.
The
.B v7as
command performs pass 1, then executes
.B v7as2
(pass 2) to write the object file; users normally invoke only
.BR v7as .
.PP
Input is the historical V7
.I as
syntax: instructions and addressing modes are written as on the PDP-11,
numbers are octal unless terminated by a decimal point, and strings are
delimited by
.BI < >\c
\&.  The statements
.BR .text ,
.BR .data ,
.BR .bss ,
.BR .globl ,
.BR .comm ,
and
.B .byte
are recognised, as are numeric labels
.RI ( n: ,
.RI n f,
.RI n b).
.PP
The output is a V7
.I a.out
file (magic 0407) with the standard 8-word header, text, data, relocation
and symbol tables.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-
.TP
.B \-u
Treat undefined symbols as external (global) rather than as errors.  The
two spellings are equivalent.
.TP
.BI \-o " objfile"
Name the output file
.I objfile
instead of
.BR a.out .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B a.out
output object file
.TP
.B /tmp/atm1a /tmp/atm2a /tmp/atm3a
intermediate files passed from pass 1 to pass 2
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics are written to the standard output, one per error, in the
historical one-line form
.RI ( "name? line" ).
.SH HISTORY
This is a faithful C translation of the V7 assembler, kept for use as a
cross-assembler in the koitix toolchain.  The
.B .s
originals remain in the source tree as the conformance oracle.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v7ld (1),
.IR nm (1),
.IR a.out (5)
